      "Raw device bytes reaching any holder, or a holder-selectable algorithm, seed or reseed policy.";
      "Running Nav2, any ROS 2 workload, or a bun-compiled binary; C++ and language-runtime support (exceptions, .eh_frame retention, TLS, libc, JIT memory) is separate work.";
      "Sharing or demand-mapping read-only segments from root image frames instead of copying them.";
      "Read-only data-object grants for maps or other assets.";
      "The 1 GiB MEM-ADAPTIVE inventory row; the large-image composition boots on the profile's default 2 GiB.";
      "Generations loaded from the boot store (boot_selector's 4 MiB buffer), riscv64, x86-64, rpi5, Framework, or any 12-bit root CNode target, which keep the 512-page ceiling.";
      "Physical-machine evidence; QEMU evidence carries no hardware claim.";
      "Badge-based emptiness: the root mints peer endpoints with badge 0, so a real message can carry badge 0 and the badge cannot mean empty.";
      "Changing the blocking receive path or the message wire format.";
      "The Zenoh QEMU exchange; it is blocked by this defect but is graded by its own item.";
      "No relaxation, reconstruction, deletion or normalization of broken serial markers to obtain a pass; original failure markers and causal ordering remain enforced.";
      "No receive repair changes, network protocol changes, physical-machine qualification or claims that the missing original failure transcript has been recovered.";
