      "Waking network-service on link completion notifications. That is a separate item.";
      "The seL4 kernel's own debug messages, SLIME_CLOCK expired lines and every other root diagnostic.";
      "A build-time or generation-declared switch for root diagnostics.";
      "Physical NIC or board qualification. QEMU evidence carries no hardware claim.";
      "A throughput target. Client requests already wake the service while a stream is being sent; this item removes the timer-paced handling of frames that arrive with no request pending.";
      "Compositions whose network-service has no wait set or no virtio-net driver, which keep the polling profile or the loopback backend.";
      "Changing the service's 10 ms idle timer.";
      "The root's per-operation diagnostic lines, which 01a1728d-a7d7-7343-b9ae-b3a827b8012e owns.";
      "Relaxing, reconstructing or normalizing split markers in any checker to obtain a pass.";
      "Changing root diagnostics or the root and console serialization, which 01a11bda-7038-7b80-8963-ae49bf9ce922 owns.";
